WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.128
When Mary Lennox was sent to Misselthwaite Manor to live with her uncle, everyone said she was the most disagreeable-looking child ever seen.

2
00:00:10.128 --> 00:00:11.706
It was true too.

3
00:00:11.706 --> 00:00:17.415
She had a thin, little face; a thin, little body; and thin, blond hair.

4
00:00:17.415 --> 00:00:25.459
She had a sour look on her face, and her skin was pale because she had always been sick.

5
00:00:25.459 --> 00:00:30.367
She had been born in India, where her father worked for the English government.

6
00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:36.943
Her mother was a great beauty who only wanted to go to parties and amuse herself with interesting people.

7
00:00:36.943 --> 00:00:40.078
She had not wanted a little girl at all.

8
00:00:40.078 --> 00:00:45.136
So when Mary was born, her mother handed her over to the care of a nanny.

9
00:00:45.136 --> 00:00:51.175
The nanny had strict instructions: Keep the baby out of sight as much as possible.

10
00:00:51.175 --> 00:00:58.085
The servants always let Mary do whatever she wanted to keep her from crying and making her mother angry.

11
00:00:58.085 --> 00:01:03.120
By the time Mary was six years old, she was very selfish and stubborn.

12
00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.036
A young English governess came to teach her to read and write.

13
00:01:07.036 --> 00:01:11.884
But she disliked Mary so much that she stayed only three months.

14
00:01:11.884 --> 00:01:16.388
Other governesses came and went even faster.

15
00:01:16.388 --> 00:01:21.994
One very hot morning, when she was about ten, Mary awoke feeling grumpy.

16
00:01:21.994 --> 00:01:28.276
She was even grumpier when she saw that the woman standing by her bed was not her usual nanny.

17
00:01:28.276 --> 00:01:31.619
"Why are you here?" she said to the strange woman.

18
00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:35.336
"I will not let you stay. Send my nanny to me."

19
00:01:35.336 --> 00:01:40.012
The woman looked frightened. "She cannot come."

20
00:01:40.012 --> 00:01:44.213
Mary flew into a rage and beat and kicked the servant.

21
00:01:44.213 --> 00:01:49.235
But the frightened woman would only repeat, "The nanny cannot come."

22
00:01:49.235 --> 00:01:55.220
"There is a mystery in the air this morning," said Mary to herself after the servant went away.

23
00:01:55.220 --> 00:02:00.299
As she walked about the house, she noticed that some of the servants were missing.

24
00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:03.829
The ones that she did see looked frightened.

25
00:02:03.829 --> 00:02:08.887
She went out into the garden and began to play under a tree near the porch.

26
00:02:08.887 --> 00:02:13.239
"I can pretend to make a flower garden," said Mary.

27
00:02:13.239 --> 00:02:21.603
She stuck big, red hibiscus blossoms into little heaps of earth, but still felt angry that her nanny had abandoned her.

28
00:02:21.603 --> 00:02:24.736
Suddenly someone came out on the porch.

29
00:02:24.736 --> 00:02:28.039
It was her mother and a young English soldier.

30
00:02:28.039 --> 00:02:33.385
Her mother's face and clothes were as beautiful as ever, but something was wrong.

31
00:02:33.385 --> 00:02:35.778
Mary's mother looked upset.

32
00:02:35.778 --> 00:02:40.764
"Is it so very bad? Oh, is it?" Mary heard her ask.

33
00:02:40.764 --> 00:02:43.173
"Awful," said the young soldier.

34
00:02:43.173 --> 00:02:46.454
"You ought to have gone to the hills two weeks ago."

35
00:02:46.454 --> 00:02:49.687
Mary did not know what they were talking about.

36
00:02:49.687 --> 00:02:52.300
She stayed quiet and listened.

37
00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:56.267
"Oh, I know I should have gone," said Mary's mother.

38
00:02:56.267 --> 00:03:01.276
"I only stayed to go to that silly party. What a fool I was!"

39
00:03:01.276 --> 00:03:05.445
Suddenly the sound of wailing came from the servants' quarters.

40
00:03:05.445 --> 00:03:08.684
The noise grew louder and wilder.

41
00:03:08.684 --> 00:03:12.081
"What is that?" cried Mary's mother.

42
00:03:12.081 --> 00:03:15.278
"Someone has died," said the soldier.

43
00:03:15.278 --> 00:03:18.691
"You did not tell me it had broken out among your servants."

44
00:03:18.691 --> 00:03:23.599
"I did not know," said Mary's mother. "Come with me!"

45
00:03:23.599 --> 00:03:27.171
And she ran into the house with the soldier.

46
00:03:27.171 --> 00:03:30.736
Mary soon learned why the servants were wailing.

47
00:03:30.736 --> 00:03:37.445
Her nanny had died of cholera, a dreaded disease that was spreading quickly and killing many people.

48
00:03:37.445 --> 00:03:44.147
By the next day, three more servants were dead, and the others had run away in terror.

49
00:03:44.147 --> 00:03:51.046
During the confusion of the following day, Mary hid in the nursery and was forgotten by everyone.

50
00:03:51.046 --> 00:03:54.764
Nobody thought of her and nobody wanted her.

51
00:03:54.764 --> 00:03:58.842
Mary alternately cried and slept through the hours.

52
00:03:58.842 --> 00:04:02.556
When she awoke the house was perfectly quiet.

53
00:04:02.556 --> 00:04:06.810
"I wonder if everyone is better," Mary said.

54
00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:14.040
She heard something rustling on the floor, and when she looked down, she saw a little snake gliding along.

55
00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.973
"It sounds as if no one is here but the snake and me."

56
00:04:17.973 --> 00:04:22.684
The next minute she heard footsteps on the porch and voices in the house.

57
00:04:22.684 --> 00:04:26.638
Mary jumped out of bed as a soldier came into her room.

58
00:04:26.638 --> 00:04:31.412
"There is a child here!" he called to the other soldiers in the house.

59
00:04:31.412 --> 00:04:35.746
"A child alone! In a place like this! Who is she?"

60
00:04:35.746 --> 00:04:38.958
"I am Mary Lennox," she said.

61
00:04:38.958 --> 00:04:42.951
"I fell asleep when everyone had cholera, and I just woke up.

62
00:04:42.951 --> 00:04:47.088
Why was I forgotten? Why does no one come?"

63
00:04:47.088 --> 00:04:53.445
The soldier looked at her sadly. "Because there is no one left to come."

64
00:04:53.445 --> 00:05:01.670
So it was in this strange and sudden way that Mary found out that both her father and mother had died of cholera.

65
00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:10.958
There was no one left in the house but Mary and the little, rustling snake.

